@startuml storage-layout
' Unghosted — file storage layout + envelope encryption
title Unghosted — file storage and encryption

skinparam linetype ortho

storage "Local filesystem (dev, CI, staging)\nvolume: /var/lib/unghosted/storage" as local {
  folder "users/{userId}/documents/{documentId}.bin" as l1
  folder "users/{userId}/exports/{exportJobId}.bin" as l2
}

storage "AWS S3 (production)\nbucket: unghosted-documents (private)" as s3 {
  folder "users/{userId}/documents/{documentId}.bin" as s1
  folder "users/{userId}/exports/{exportJobId}.bin" as s2
}

card "Storage gateway (interface)" as gateway
cloud "AWS KMS (prod) / config key (dev, staging)" as kms

gateway .. local : configuration selects
gateway .. s3 : configuration selects
s3 .. kms : master key decrypt/encrypt data keys

note right of gateway
  Contract test suite shared by both implementations:
  write, read as stream, delete, missing-key, large file.
  S3 tested in CI with moto (in-process); real-bucket
  smoke test only in the AWS deploy pipeline.
end note

note bottom of local
  No S3-compatible server in dev (ADR 0001):
  storage is behind the interface, so a local volume
  exercises the same code path minus the HTTP transport.
end note

card "Envelope encryption (identical both backends)" as enc {
  card "file content" as content
  card "random data key (AES-256-GCM)\nencrypts content" as datakey
  card "master key encrypts data key" as wrap
  content <- datakey
  datakey <- wrap
}

enc .. gateway : encrypted bytes only reach storage

note bottom of enc
  documents.encrypted_data_key + key_algorithm_version
  stored in Postgres. Same mechanism as OAuth tokens.
  Files served only via API download endpoint:
  ownership check every request, decrypted stream,
  never presigned URLs, never inline from app origin.
end note
@enduml
